. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.         * Example: only keep people with at least one child
.         keep if kidsex01==1 | kidsex01==2
(216,893 observations deleted)

.         keep if syear==2018
(419,815 observations deleted)

. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.                 * left leaning political preferences
. gen left_pol=0 if plh0333!=. 
(5,832 missing values generated)

. replace left_pol=. if plh0333==-1 |plh0333==-5|plh0333==-8
(4,234 real changes made, 4,234 to missing)

. replace left_pol=1 if plh0333==1 | plh0333==5 | plh0333==6 | plh0333==15 |plh
> 0333==16
(5,589 real changes made)

. 
. 
.         * gender 1st child
. gen daughter=1 if kidsex01==2
(13,512 missing values generated)

. replace daughter=0 if kidsex01==1
(13,512 real changes made)

. 
.         * gender respondent
. gen father=1 if sex==1
(14,533 missing values generated)

. replace father=0 if sex==2
(14,533 real changes made)

.         
.         * number of children: sumkids (not recoded)
. 
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * I run an OLS model where we study whether gender of the first child
>  (daughter) impacts left leaning political preferences (left_pol), hence the 
> variable of interest is daughter.
.         * Since gen_att is only measured in 2019 the regression is automatica
> lly only based on data from 2019
. 
.         reg left_pol daughter sex sumkids       

      Source |       SS           df       MS      Number of obs   =    16,349
-------------+----------------------------------   F(3, 16345)     =      8.36
       Model |  5.63621136         3  1.87873712   Prob > F        =    0.0000
    Residual |  3672.73188    16,345  .224700635   R-squared       =    0.0015
-------------+----------------------------------   Adj R-squared   =    0.0013
       Total |   3678.3681    16,348  .225004165   Root MSE        =    .47403

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    left_pol | Coefficient  Std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
    daughter |   -.007925   .0074168    -1.07   0.285    -.0224628    .0066129
         sex |   .0053242   .0074799     0.71   0.477    -.0093373    .0199857
     sumkids |  -.0170535   .0035124    -4.86   0.000    -.0239382   -.0101689
       _cons |   .3739521   .0147549    25.34   0.000     .3450309    .4028732
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * (Please check whether the suggested code autom
> atically picks up the correct statistics for your chosen regression analysis 
> and adapt if needed)
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[daughter] / _se[daughter]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 scalar coef_daughter = _b[daughter]

.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
